# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions for DOLFINx DeveloperDebug builds.
#
# Use with: UBSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=<path-to-this-file>
#
# NOTE: on macOS/Apple Clang the runtime suppression mechanism does not
# reliably honour "null" or "alignment" checks by file/function glob (tested
# against LLVM 17's Darwin UBSan runtime, which supports a narrower
# suppression set than the Linux runtime). Where a runtime suppression does
# not take effect, disable the specific check at compile time instead, e.g.
# with a file-scoped `#pragma clang attribute` or `-fsanitize-ignorelist=`
# entry local to the affected translation unit.
#
# Empty by default. Add entries as false positives are found in
# non-DOLFINx code, e.g.:
#   nonnull-attribute:libsome-dependency
